{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466512",
      "title": "Preloading Lazy-Loaded Code",
      "lectureOrder": 659,
      "videoOrder": 607,
      "sourceHash": "c3233971b084b357d2951a2734b76b588acbc32322c9c13e9f4c95beb864d007",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.28,
          "end": 5.91,
          "en": "-: I mentioned a way of optimizing lazy loading,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.91,
          "end": 8.91,
          "en": "which itself of course is already an optimization.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.91,
          "end": 13.8,
          "en": "And with it, I mean how the lazy loaded code is then loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.8,
          "end": 16.38,
          "en": "Right now we load code whenever we need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.38,
          "end": 20.16,
          "en": "So as soon as we visit /recipes, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.16,
          "end": 24.9,
          "en": "after logging in, we bring in the recipes module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.9,
          "end": 26.31,
          "en": "Now the downside of that of course, is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.31,
          "end": 28.95,
          "en": "that this is downloaded in parts just when we need it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.95,
          "end": 32.34,
          "en": "leading to a very tiny delay in our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.34,
          "end": 35.64,
          "en": "We might not see that here because the module is small",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.64,
          "end": 37.92,
          "en": "and the internet connection is fast,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.92,
          "end": 39.18,
          "en": "but the bigger the module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.18,
          "end": 42.03,
          "en": "and the slower the internet connection, or for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.03,
          "end": 44.64,
          "en": "if you temporary have no internet connection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.64,
          "end": 46.89,
          "en": "the longer that delay will be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.89,
          "end": 49.83,
          "en": "And therefore we can actually tell angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.83,
          "end": 54.83,
          "en": "to preload lazy loaded modules to avoid this delay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.03,
          "end": 60.24,
          "en": "For this we simply go to our root router module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.24,
          "end": 62.67,
          "en": "So here where we configure our root routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.67,
          "end": 65.463,
          "en": "and you can pass a second argument to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.39,
          "end": 69.81,
          "en": "This is an object where you can configure that route router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.81,
          "end": 73.86,
          "en": "and there you can set up a pre-loading strategy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.86,
          "end": 78.27,
          "en": "and you can set this equal to preload all modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.27,
          "end": 79.59,
          "en": "Default is no pre-loading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.59,
          "end": 81.03,
          "en": "You don't need to set this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.03,
          "end": 84.03,
          "en": "but you can set this to preload all modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.03,
          "end": 86.31,
          "en": "which is simply and in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.31,
          "end": 89.64,
          "en": "a constant you need to import from @angler router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.64,
          "end": 90.473,
          "en": "Speaking of imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.473,
          "end": 92.7,
          "en": "you should remove the off component import, by the way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.7,
          "end": 95.31,
          "en": "to optimize lazy loading as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.31,
          "end": 97.56,
          "en": "But with preload all modules imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.56,
          "end": 99.57,
          "en": "and set here as a pre-loading strategy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.57,
          "end": 101.58,
          "en": "you're telling angler, well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.58,
          "end": 104.22,
          "en": "generally we're using lazy loading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.22,
          "end": 107.07,
          "en": "so it will not put all the code into one bundle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.07,
          "end": 109.56,
          "en": "It will split it as we saw it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.56,
          "end": 113.85,
          "en": "but it will preload the bundles as soon as possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.85,
          "end": 115.65,
          "en": "So when we are on the off page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.65,
          "end": 118.65,
          "en": "it will already preload recipes and shopping list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.65,
          "end": 121.68,
          "en": "so that these code bundles are already available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.68,
          "end": 122.88,
          "en": "when we need them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 125.64,
          "en": "The advantage is that the initial download bundle still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.64,
          "end": 129,
          "en": "is kept small because there that code is not included",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129,
          "end": 132.51,
          "en": "and therefore the initial loading phase is fast.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.51,
          "end": 134.97,
          "en": "But then when the user is browsing the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.97,
          "end": 138.3,
          "en": "and therefore has we have some idle time anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.3,
          "end": 141.96,
          "en": "then we preload these additional code bundles to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.96,
          "end": 145.07999999999998,
          "en": "that subsequent navigation requests are faster.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.07999999999998,
          "end": 148.86,
          "en": "So we're getting the best of both worlds a fast initial load",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.86,
          "end": 152.28,
          "en": "and thereafter fast subsequent loads.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.28,
          "end": 154.53,
          "en": "So with that pre-loading strategy set up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.53,
          "end": 157.14,
          "en": "now if we reload this page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.14,
          "end": 159.32999999999998,
          "en": "you actually see something interesting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 159.32999999999998,
          "end": 163.89,
          "en": "We of course see that well the main js file on is loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.89,
          "end": 168.89,
          "en": "but then we all see that here the recipes module is loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.59,
          "end": 171.93,
          "en": "and the shopping list module is loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.93,
          "end": 173.82,
          "en": "and therefore now if I clear this all here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 173.82,
          "end": 176.553,
          "en": "the network request output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 177.42000000000002,
          "end": 179.46,
          "en": "you see no downloads of these modules here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.46,
          "end": 182.13,
          "en": "because they already were preloaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.13,
          "end": 184.65,
          "en": "Still we had that smaller initial bundle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 184.65,
          "end": 187.08,
          "en": "but we benefit from these code packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 187.08,
          "end": 189.42,
          "en": "being there when we need them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 189.42,
          "end": 191.43,
          "en": "And therefore setting this pre-loading strategy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 191.43,
          "end": 193.38,
          "en": "is definitely worth of thought",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 193.38,
          "end": 195.48,
          "en": "if you wanna optimize lazy loading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 195.48,
          "end": 199.02,
          "en": "and you wanna ensure that this goes as fast as possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 199.02,
          "end": 202.8,
          "en": "Now you can even build your own pre-loading strategies here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 202.8,
          "end": 205.26,
          "en": "where you could have more refined logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 205.26,
          "end": 207.84,
          "en": "for example controlling that only certain routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 207.84,
          "end": 209.01,
          "en": "should be pre-loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 209.01,
          "end": 212.07,
          "en": "but that is beyond the scope of that course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 212.07,
          "end": 215.52,
          "en": "Being aware of that pre-loading strategy is super important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 215.52,
          "end": 217.52,
          "en": "though and that is how you could use it.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
